Scope of Variables :
    it is used when  inside the function declaration variables are not accessed by outside of the function.
      * local variable
      * global variable

local variable :
         variable which are defined inside the block or inside the function is called local variable.
Global variable : 
             the variable can be accessed from anywhere.
     Example :
          // function for odd or even using function
               function oddEven(n){
                    if(n%2 == 0){
                         return "even";
                           }
                         return "odd";  ---> it executes and come out of the block and wont execute the remaining parts.
                }
              console.log(oddEven(22));
--------------------------------------------------------------------
function declaration :
          assigning the function to the variable.
          after writing the function , it assign to the variable.
     Example :
         // function for odd or even using function
               function oddEven(n){
                    if(n%2 == 0){
                         return "even";
                           }
                         return "odd";   // ---> it executes and come out of the block and wont execute the remaining parts.
                }
                let oddEv = oddEven;
                console.log(oddEv(22));


          // function assigning to variable :
            let oddEven = function (n){
                    if(n%2 == 0){
                         return "even";
                           }
                         return "odd";   // ---> it executes and come out of the block and wont execute the remaining parts.
                }
                
              console.log(oddEven(22)); 
